From: microvm <microvm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/sparsemem: use 32 MB memory sections

memmap_init() initialises struct pages up to the end of the last memory
section, past the end of RAM, because early sections are pfn_valid() for
their whole span. With 128 MB sections a 64 MB guest touches 2 MB of
memory map instead of 1 MB, and a 32 MB guest 2 MB instead of 0.5 MB.
32 MB sections bound that waste at 0.5 MB; the price is a larger zeroed
mem_section root table (64 KB instead of 16 KB with 4-level paging).

--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/sparsemem.h	2026-11-04 07:47:26.616415183 +0100
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/sparsemem.h	2026-11-04 07:47:26.632247388 +0100
@@ -25,7 +25,14 @@
 #  define MAX_PHYSMEM_BITS	32
 # endif
 #else /* CONFIG_X86_32 */
-# define SECTION_SIZE_BITS	27 /* matt - 128 is convenient right now */
+/*
+ * 32 MB sections: the memory map of the last section is initialised up to
+ * the section end even past the end of RAM, so 128 MB sections cost a
+ * 64 MB microVM 1 MB of struct pages it doesn't have. Smaller sections
+ * grow the zeroed mem_section root table instead (64 KB with 4-level
+ * paging).
+ */
+# define SECTION_SIZE_BITS	25
 # define MAX_PHYSMEM_BITS	(pgtable_l5_enabled() ? 52 : 46)
 #endif
 
